# HTML 24.4% (Linengrow web glass / gratitude .html): product-vs-sketch is Kaeden's
# per-path word — left unmarked until that ruling. Shell (.rish/.sh) stays as-is.

# Day-shelf indexes take one prepended row from EVERY seat, so any two clones
# that both landed laps conflict at the same line on every rebase (Mind's
# first cured lap hit it, 20260830.000121). This carried merge=union until
# 20260908, on the reading that order was cosmetic and a stamp-order reseat
# would ride on touch. Order is not cosmetic -- the page promises NEWEST
# FIRST -- and union concatenates in hunk order, so a rebase whose own row is
# newer seats the older row on top. REDS %440 fired fourteen-plus times that
# way, each repaired by hand, because every ship that pulls re-earns it.
# merge=dayshelf unions the same rows and reseats them in stamp order, and
# refuses rather than guesses on a shape it cannot read. The driver's command
# line lives in git config, which no clone inherits, so a fresh clone must run
# `rishi/bin/rishi run tools/i/install_hooks.rish` -- until it does, the shelf
# conflicts visibly rather than merging wrong.
# Driver: tools/d/dayshelf_merge.sh -- proven by tools/d/dayshelf_merge_witness.rish
session-logs/date/README-index-*.md merge=dayshelf
